   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable, independent of the author): APPROVE**, head 7156e55\n\nVerified against the CI logs. On the red run (0e0f61a), about 50 plain model tests reported 67–100 s and the two web tests failed at 95–102 s. On the previous green run (bfb58f2), the same tests took about 10 s. A 90 s deadline counted from the call is used up by the parallel run's warm-up.\n- No `until` expects `false`, so nothing slows down when the tests pass.\n- `settled()` inherits the new deadline.\n- The app job has no `timeout-minutes`. The worst case is about 1.5 h, under GitHub's 360 min.\n- No test is skipped or weakened.\n\nTwo non-blocking findings, both left as they are:\n1. **Low.** When WebKit never gets ready, a test keeps waiting after its first failed `until` (up to 12 min per test). The fix is `try #require(await until { recorder.ready == [1] })` on the first wait. It would be a follow-up on the reader tests, outside this CI unblock.\n2. **Info.** In the doc comment, the 70–100 s is the warm-up of the whole parallel run, not only WebKit's start. The number and the fix are the same, so the wording stays. Changing it now would restart the 10-minute app job that `dev-swift` is waiting on.\n\nMerge once the PR's `App build + tests` job is green.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
